showcase.message.output.inline.file.link.body=Commands\n\n- `bazel test //...` — JUnit 5, Vitest, TypeScript type-check, and ESLint.\n- `bazel build //:zodiac_deploy.jar` — JVM fat JAR with the frontend.\n- `bazel run //:backend` — backend on port 8080.\n- `bazel run //frontend:dev` — Vite with HMR on port 5173.\n- `java -jar bazel-bin/zodiac_deploy.jar` — production launch without Maven or Node.js.
showcase.message.output.line.range.link.body=Supported file-reference forms render together on this page. Line ranges keep the complete range clickable and navigate to their first line.\n\nProse auto-links\n\n- File: plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt\n- Line: plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt:79\n- Line and column: plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt:79:5\n- Line range: plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt:79-87\n- Directory: plugins/air/spec/\n\nInline code links\n\n- `plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt`\n- `plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt:79`\n- `plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt:79:5`\n- Range starting inside rendered KDoc: `plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/ui/markdown/links/LinkOpenTarget.kt:242-255`\n\nFenced code links\n\n```text\nplugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt\nplugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt:79\nplugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt:79:5\nplugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/references/FileReferenceLinkDetector.kt:79-87\n```
showcase.message.output.code.wrap.body=Long fenced lines preserve their whitespace and soft-wrap inside the chat column.\n\n```kotlin\nval resolvedConfiguration = sessionConfiguration.copy(model = selectedModel, reasoningEffort = selectedReasoningEffort, accessMode = selectedAccessMode, projectDirectory = resolvedProjectDirectory, environment = inheritedEnvironment + launchEnvironment + mapOf("AIR_SHOWCASE_LONG_CONFIGURATION_KEY" to "a deliberately long value that keeps this Kotlin source line wider than the showcase preview"))\n```\n\n```json\n{"method":"thread/start","params":{"threadId":"showcase-thread-with-a-deliberately-long-identifier","cwd":"/workspace/plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui.showcase","approvalPolicy":"on-request","sandbox":{"type":"workspace-write","writableRoots":["/workspace/plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui.showcase","/workspace/plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui","/workspace/plugins/air/spec/core"]},"note":"This compact JSON payload intentionally remains on one authored line so the preview demonstrates fenced-code soft wrapping."}}\n```
showcase.message.output.inline.wrap.body=Updated plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/src/ui/markdown/ExtraordinarilyLongMarkdownFileReferencePresentationFactory.kt and verified plugins/air/frontend/session/view.gui/testSrc/ui/markdown/ExtraordinarilyLongMarkdownFileReferencePresentationFactoryIntegrationTest.kt. The surrounding explanation deliberately contains enough ordinary words to wrap before and after both long file-name links without widening or clipping the message.\n\nThe same row also contains `an inline code fragment with many separate words that must wrap naturally inside the available chat column instead of forcing the complete paragraph off screen`, followed by ordinary prose that must remain visible after the inline fragment wraps.

